    {
      "id": "1pr9gyp",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "8. TYPES OF TAX RATES"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "7ie6jbs",
      "content": "Progressive Tax – Rate increases with income.<br></br>Regressive Tax – Rate decreases as income rises.<br></br>Proportional Tax – Same rate for all income levels.<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "j6ix3kn",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Type</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Meaning</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Progressive</p>",
            "<p>Rate increases with income</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Regressive</p>",
            "<p>Rate decreases as income rises</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Proportional</p>",
            "<p>Same rate for all incomes</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "3noz142",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "9. TAX ADMINISTRATION IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "uii7dib",
      "content": "• CBDT – Direct taxes administration.<br></br>• CBIC – Indirect taxes administration.<br></br>• GST Council – Decides GST rates and structure.<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "82fe4f5",
      "content": "<strong>10. TAX-TO-GDP RATIO &amp; TAX BUOYANCY</strong>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "05fx4p9",
      "content": "Tax-to-GDP Ratio measures tax revenue as percentage of GDP.<br></br>Higher ratio indicates better revenue mobilisation.<br></br><br></br>Tax Buoyancy measures responsiveness of tax revenue to changes in GDP."
    },
