    {
      "id": "mpjlxey",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. GST COUNCIL – STRUCTURE & VOTING PATTERN"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yzzyyd9",
      "content": "GST Council was established under Article 279A of the Constitution."
    },
    {
      "id": "wad57iv",
      "type": "table",
      "rows": [
        {
          "isHeader": true,
          "cells": [
            "<p><strong>Position</strong></p>",
            "<p><strong>Details</strong></p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Chairperson</p>",
            "<p>Union Finance Minister</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Members</p>",
            "<p>Union MoS (Finance) + State Finance Ministers</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Quorum</p>",
            "<p>50% of total members</p>"
          ]
        },
        {
          "isHeader": false,
          "cells": [
            "<p>Decision Rule</p>",
            "<p>75% weighted majority</p>"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "wml8bml",
      "content": "Voting Pattern:"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently test the voting weightage in the GST Council: Centre gets 33.33% (1/3rd) weightage and States get 66.67% (2/3rd) weightage, requiring a 75% (3/4th) majority to pass any resolution.",
        "Distinguish clearly between Tax Elasticity (growth without policy changes) and Tax Buoyancy (growth including discretionary policy changes).",
        "Direct taxes are progressive in nature (reducing income inequality), whereas indirect taxes are considered regressive as they impact all income groups equally."
      ],
      "id": "e1fsvgc"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "vykqeza",
      "content": "• Centre’s vote weight = 1/3<br></br>• States’ combined vote weight = 2/3<br></br>• Decision requires 3/4th majority of weighted votes<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "f8r77mz",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. TAX BUOYANCY & TAX-TO-GDP RATIO"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6ngbjh9",
      "content": "Tax-to-GDP Ratio = (Total Tax Revenue / GDP) × 100<br></br>It measures the efficiency of tax collection relative to economic size."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c2q1v65",
      "content": "Tax Buoyancy measures responsiveness of tax revenue to changes in GDP.<br></br>Formula: % Change in Tax Revenue / % Change in GDP<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "muccet7",
      "content": "If Tax Buoyancy &gt; 1 → Tax revenue grows faster than GDP.<br></br>If Tax Buoyancy &lt; 1 → Tax revenue grows slower than GDP.<br></br>"
    },
    {
      "id": "05udj8v",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "RRB HIGH-VALUE POINTS"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "oelivsi",
      "content": "• New tax regime is default.<br></br>• GST Council formed under Article 279A.<br></br>• Centre has 1/3 voting power.<br></br>• Tax-to-GDP ratio shows fiscal capacity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "6ti46jb",
      "content": "• GST is destination-based tax.<br></br>• Direct tax burden cannot be shifted.<br></br>• Progressive tax promotes equity.<br></br>• GST implemented on 1 July 2017.<br></br>"
    }
  ],
